This is Hidden Brain. I'm Shankar Vedantam. In the early days of Soviet cinema, a filmmaker conducted an experiment that would change our understanding of the human mind. Lev Kulishav showed an audience a short film featuring a famous actor. The footage of the actor was always the same, a single, unmoving, and entirely neutral expression. But the filmmaker intercut the shot with three different images. A bowl of hot soup, a child in a coffee. and a woman reclining on a sofa. Even though the actor's face never changed,
这里是《隐藏的大脑》。我是尚卡尔·维丹塔姆。在苏联电影的早期，一位电影制作人进行了一项实验，这项实验改变了我们对人类思维的理解。列夫·库里肖夫向观众展示了一部短片，片中有一位著名演员。演员的镜头始终如一，是一个单一、静止且完全中性的表情。但这位电影制作人将这个镜头与三个不同的画面剪辑在一起：一碗热汤、一个孩子和一口棺材，以及一个躺在沙发上的女人。尽管演员的脸从未改变，

